{"id": "EUVD-2026-91478", "enisaUuid": "40cc44ef-1e35-3991-88a8-ff425228ceeb", "description": "YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in ApiService::isAuthorized() that allows unauthenticated attackers to call admin-only API routes when public API mode is enabled. Attackers can send requests to endpoints like api/ci/update_config and api/archives to overwrite configuration and list, download, or delete backup archives.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T15:15:54", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-v527-6r4j-j2w2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-authorization-bypass-via-public-api-mode"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104467", "GHSA-59xh-vh54-x5hf"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "af330a2d-4202-3f21-9696-7d6687c38482", "product": {"name": "yeswiki", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9c151576-9d83-379b-ac57-a9a3d07125b1", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}], "isExploited": false}